    "result_text": "The full suite is green. Only the `AcceptanceTest` class contains actual `@Test` methods (the other two files are the `AcceptanceBase` harness and support), so all tests ran and passed.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the collision de-duplication in `customerCode(Owner)` in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java:305`.\n\nThe method still builds the base code as `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, but now:\n1. Collects the set of existing owners' non-null `customerCode`s.\n2. Returns the base code unchanged if it's unique.\n3. Otherwise appends `-<n>`, starting at `n=2` and incrementing until the result is unique (e.g. `NSW-1A2B3C4D-2`, then `-3`, \u2026), and returns that de-duplicated code.\n\nThis satisfies the spec \u2014 smallest `n \u2265 2` that makes the code unique \u2014 and the `coreCustomerCodesStayUnique` acceptance test passes, with `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
